      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It would be extremely nice if you could define your avatar descriptor using a point (like we do for enter/exit location of chairs), which would also allow animating of the IPD as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-29T06:36:31.526Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The idea is pretty simple, this would be similar to the normal avatar descriptor but have some options that most people wouldn't need to touch. Things like potentially using manual IPD scale, custom animator support, leg IK distance(kinda goes with the manual IPD), standing height modifier(in the case you want your legs to purposely be bent slightly when standing normally without doing some odd shenanigans to the model), custom final ik (within reason), and maybe some other features i can't think of at the moment.",
